{{!
  Klabis customization: a verbatim fork of the stock JavaSpring pathParams.mustache with ONE
  addition — the x-klabis-target-id section below, which emits @TargetId on the generated interface
  method's parameter.

  Rationale: @TargetId names the parameter holding the ID of the target the operation is about, so
  that an authority held only over specific targets and @OwnerVisible on the operation have
  something to resolve against. It used to reach the generator as
  x-field-extra-annotation, stamped on during bundling, which also forced the bundler to inline
  any shared $ref parameter so the annotation landed on one operation only. Reading the key here
  instead means the annotation can sit on the shared parameter: @TargetId is inert on its own —
  the evaluator only consults it for a method or field that is already guarded by an authority or
  marked @OwnerVisible.

  Maintenance: this is a vendor fork and nothing detects drift. On an openapi-generator upgrade,
  diff it against the new stock JavaSpring/pathParams.mustache and port the addition across.
}}
